Build-Depends-Arch: cargo
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/nubian-ibex/ibexwall

Package: ibexwall
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, nftables, polkitd | policykit-1, systemd
Suggests: chrony, ufw | firewalld
Description: Security center for Linux
 IbexWall shows how secure a Linux computer is, explains what to fix, and
 fixes it with changes you review first and can undo. This package holds the
 daemon, the command line, the resolver and the plugins; nothing it does is
 applied without a plan, a snapshot and your approval.

Package: ibexwall-desktop
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, ibexwall (= ${binary:Version}), libwebkit2gtk-4.1-0, libgtk-3-0
Recommends: libayatana-appindicator3-1
Description: IbexWall desktop app and session agent
 The IbexWall window and tray icon, and the agent that asks you about a held
 connection.

Package: ibexwall-mcp
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, ibexwall (= ${binary:Version})
Description: IbexWall MCP server for AI assistants
 The MCP server that lets an AI assistant read your security status and
 suggest changes. It can never apply one. The HTTPS mode is off until you
 turn it on.
